Package: mini-cmts
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: BILLY Rémi <byhoster.association@gmail.com>
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-numpy, python3-scipy, gcc, libc6-dev, iproute2, sudo, adduser
Recommends: python3-uhd, uhd-host
Suggests: bladerf, libbladerf2, bladerf-fpga-hostedxa4, tshark, iperf3
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: DOCSIS 3.0 CMTS on a software radio (USRP B210, bladeRF 2.0 micro)
 A cable modem termination system written in Python and C for a closed coax
 lab: EuroDOCSIS downstream (J.83 annex A, 64/256-QAM, channel bonding up to
 6 channels per B210, several B210s) and upstream (TDMA / ATDMA up to 64-QAM,
 multiple transmit channels), ranging, registration, BPI-less data path
 bridged to a Linux TAP, DHCP / TFTP / ToD provisioning, status page.
 .
 License: AGPL-3.0-only, or a commercial licence (COMMERCIAL.md).
 .
 Tested with a Sagem F@st 3686 (DOCSIS 3.0). Never connect it to an
 operator's network: closed lab, with attenuators.
 .
 The C kernels are compiled at installation for the CPU of this machine
 (dpkg-reconfigure mini-cmts after moving the disk to another CPU).
